00:24:47.030 --> 00:24:49.460
where criminals take
over your computer system

00:24:49.460 --> 00:24:52.760
and request a payment in
order to decrypt the files

00:24:52.760 --> 00:24:54.660
and give you back access to your systems.

00:24:54.660 --> 00:24:56.910
So while it wasn't accurate

00:24:56.910 --> 00:24:59.635
back when the film took
place, in the '90s,

00:24:59.635 --> 00:25:01.520
I think it really predicted the future.

00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:05.310
I would love to give this 10 out of 10.

00:25:05.310 --> 00:25:07.768
I'm gonna take away two points,

00:25:07.768 --> 00:25:08.910
a couple of points,

00:25:08.910 --> 00:25:11.627
just because we don't actually see

00:25:11.627 --> 00:25:14.310
any of the software code.

00:25:14.310 --> 00:25:15.660
Stop recycling your passwords!

00:25:15.660 --> 00:25:17.150
It's not a good kind of recycling.

00:25:17.150 --> 00:25:18.380
Don't do it.

00:25:18.380 --> 00:25:20.188
In fact, I got a T-shirt somewhere

00:25:20.188 --> 00:25:23.748
that says, "Hackers don't
break in. We log in."

00:25:23.748 --> 00:25:25.316
And that's fairly accurate.

